{"metadata":{"title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"anchor":"Reference"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that observes the dispatch cycle and forwards events to a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Unlike the gate-style plugins (","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), analytics is an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"observer"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it watches actions flow by and emits events, but never blocks dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two surfaces:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mapper (passive)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — App declares a "},{"code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure once at registration. The plugin runs it in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" (explicit)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Screen views, identify\/alias\/reset, ad-hoc tracks, and opt-out toggling. For the things passive observation can’t cover cleanly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plus optional ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"auto-identify"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": pass an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keypath and the plugin watches userID transitions across dispatches, firing ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For end-to-end wiring, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Library-target","type":"heading","text":"Library target"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Provided-implementations","type":"heading","text":"Provided implementations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin ships with two in-repo conformers, both provider-agnostic and SDK-free:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MockAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — silent no-op, for previews and tests."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ConsoleAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — logs every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os.Logger"},{"type":"text","text":". Use this as the default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service:"},{"type":"text","text":" while the analytics vendor decision is still open: analytics wiring can be developed and QA-tested end to end with no SDK and no vendor commitment. Adopting a real provider later is the usual two-line change in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For production Mixpanel integrations, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package provides:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that forwards to the Mixpanel SDK and maps ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to native Mixpanel types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a Mixpanel-flavored mock for previews.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full API documentation lives in the package’s own "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For other backends (Amplitude, PostHog, Segment, custom), implement ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" Step 3, Path B.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Types","type":"heading","text":"Types"},{"level":3,"anchor":"AnalyticsPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E","type":"heading","text":"`AnalyticsPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"final class","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an action enum typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, AnalyticsState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (AnalyticsAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> AnalyticsAction?,","    service: any AnalyticsService,","    mapper: AnalyticsMapper<RootState, RootAction> = .none,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity<RootState>? = nil,","    onConsentChange: (@Sendable (Bool) async -> Void)? = nil",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fires on every ","type":"text"},{"code":".setOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dispatch with the new opted-out value. Use it to drive a vendor SDK’s own consent API — see ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Consent","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" below.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"final class"},{"type":"text","text":" (not a struct) because it tracks pending fire-and-forget service calls so that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" can deterministically await them — same reason "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are classes."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"AnalyticsState","type":"heading","text":"`AnalyticsState`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns."}]},{"code":["public struct AnalyticsState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isOptedOut: Bool","    public var currentScreen: String?","    public internal(set) var lastIdentifiedUserID: String?","","    public init(isOptedOut: Bool = false, currentScreen: String? = nil)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — App-controlled privacy flag. While ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mapper events are dropped, explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actions become no-ops, and auto-identify is paused."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — The most recent screen recorded via "},{"code":".screenView(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", auto-attached as the "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property on subsequent tracked events."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Set by the plugin (read-only from outside the module). Used to detect identity transitions.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"AnalyticsAction","type":"heading","text":"`AnalyticsAction`"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsAction: Sendable, Equatable {","    case track(AnalyticsEvent)","    case screenView(String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue])","    case alias(newID: String, previousID: String?)","    case reset","    case setOptedOut(Bool)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Convenience factories cover the common no-properties cases:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".screenView(\"Profile\")                    \/\/ properties: [:]",".identify(userID: \"u1\")                   \/\/ properties: [:]",".alias(newID: \"user-42\")                  \/\/ previousID: nil"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsEvent`","anchor":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsEvent: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var name: String","    public var properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(_ name: String, _ properties: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [:])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsValue`","anchor":"AnalyticsValue","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Closed enum keeping the protocol provider-agnostic and "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each service adapter maps these cases to its native property type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum AnalyticsValue: Sendable, Equatable {","    case string(String)","    case int(Int)","    case double(Double)","    case bool(Bool)","    case date(Date)","    case array([AnalyticsValue])","    case dict([String: AnalyticsValue])","    case null","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Literal conformances keep call-sites clean:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let props: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [","    \"amount\": 5,           \/\/ .int","    \"tier\": \"pro\",         \/\/ .string","    \"active\": true,        \/\/ .bool","    \"ratio\": 0.5,          \/\/ .double","    \"tags\": [\"a\", \"b\"],    \/\/ .array","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>`","anchor":"AnalyticsMapper%3CState-Action%3E","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wraps the declarative "},{"code":"(state, action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsMapper<State, Action>: Sendable {","    public typealias Map = @Sendable (State, Action) -> [AnalyticsEvent]","    public let map: Map","    public init(_ map: @escaping Map)","    public static var none: AnalyticsMapper { ... }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. "},{"code":".none","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default mapper for plugins that only use explicit "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsIdentity<State>`","anchor":"AnalyticsIdentity%3CState%3E","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarative source-of-truth for the active user’s identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct AnalyticsIdentity<State>: Sendable {","    public let userID: @Sendable (State) -> String?","    public let userProperties: @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue]","","    public init(","        userID: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> String?,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","","    public init(","        userID keyPath: KeyPath<State, String?> & Sendable,","        userProperties: @escaping @Sendable (State) -> [String: AnalyticsValue] = { _ in [:] }","    )","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The KeyPath convenience init is the typical shape: "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.auth.currentUserID)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`AnalyticsService` (protocol)","anchor":"AnalyticsService-protocol","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsService: Sendable {","    func track(_ event: AnalyticsEvent) async","    func identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]) async","    func alias(newID: String, previousID: String?) async","    func reset() async","    func flush() async","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementations own batching, retry, network failure handling, and offline queueing. The plugin invokes "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fire-and-forget; only "},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is awaited."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`MockAnalyticsService`","anchor":"MockAnalyticsService","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No-op conformer for previews and development."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init()","    \/\/ All methods are no-ops.","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"`ConsoleAnalyticsService`","anchor":"ConsoleAnalyticsService","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logs every "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with a recursive pretty-printer for "},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The recommended default before a vendor is chosen."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ConsoleAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init(subsystem: String = \"Swidux\", category: String = \"Analytics\")","    \/\/ Each call logs one structured line; output visible in","    \/\/ the Xcode console and Console.app, quiet in Release.","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Action semantics","anchor":"Action-semantics","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`track(AnalyticsEvent)`","anchor":"trackAnalyticsEvent","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.track(event)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" auto-attached as the "},{"code":"screen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property if the event doesn’t already specify one. Skipped entirely (returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when opted out. No state mutation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`screenView(String, properties:)`","anchor":"screenViewString-properties","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the given name "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"regardless of opt-out"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (the screen state still progresses for when the user opts back in). Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"code":"\"screen_view\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event whose properties include "},{"code":"screen_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus any extras. Skipped (returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when opted out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`identify(userID:, properties:)`","anchor":"identifyuserID-properties","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Use this when the app needs to force identity before the auto-identify keypath would observe the change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`alias(newID:, previousID:)`","anchor":"aliasnewID-previousID","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No state mutation. Returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Skipped when opted out. Call once when an anonymous user signs up to link the anonymous distinct ID to the new user ID."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`reset`","anchor":"reset","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and returns an effect calling "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Runs even when opted out — "},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is by definition a clean-slate operation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"`setOptedOut(Bool)`","anchor":"setOptedOutBool","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setOptedOut(true)"},{"type":"text","text":" — Sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut = true"},{"type":"text","text":", clears "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedUserID"},{"type":"text","text":", returns an effect that invokes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onConsentChange(true)"},{"type":"text","text":" and then calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.reset()"},{"type":"text","text":" to clear server-side identity."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setOptedOut(false)"},{"type":"text","text":" — Clears the flag. Returns an effect invoking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onConsentChange(false)"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when no hook is configured. Auto-identify on the next dispatch will re-establish identity."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Consent","anchor":"Consent","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opting out is enforced "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"plugin-side"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"screenView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the mapper, and auto-identify all return early while "},{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so nothing reaches the service. Only "},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"flush","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" still pass through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That gate stops Swidux-dispatched events. It does not touch the vendor SDK’s own consent switch — so an SDK configured to collect automatic events, or one still holding a queue of its own, can keep sending after the user opts out. "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" deliberately stays at five members (consent APIs differ too much between vendors to abstract, and only the app knows which one it is using), so the bridge is the "},{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Semantics: it fires on every "},{"code":".setOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatch with the new value, and on opt-out it runs "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the SDK’s opt-out closes the tap before the reset hands it an identity change that is still eligible to be sent. Events already in flight are not retracted."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Treat this as required wiring for any vendor with a consent API, not an optional extra: without it, “opted out” means only that Swidux stopped sending. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" Step 9 for the wiring."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Mapper semantics","anchor":"Mapper-semantics","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mapper runs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in. The plugin:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips entirely if the action is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" (handled by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" already, no double-tracking)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Skips when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.isOptedOut"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mapper.map(state, action)"},{"type":"text","text":" and tracks each returned event via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.track"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentScreen"},{"type":"text","text":" auto-attached as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen"},{"type":"text","text":" (unless the event already provides its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returning an empty array is the no-op case. The mapper closure is allowed to read freely from the post-reducer state — that’s deliberately what gets passed in."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Auto-identify semantics","anchor":"Auto-identify-semantics","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When configured with an "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the plugin re-evaluates both the "},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closures each non-analytics dispatch and diffs the pair "},{"code":"(userID, userProperties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against the last value sent to the service:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil → \"u1\""},{"type":"text","text":" (sign-in): updates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedUserID"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedProperties"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.identify(userID:\"u1\", properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"u1\" → \"u2\""},{"type":"text","text":" (account switch): updates both, fires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.identify(userID:\"u2\", properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stable userID, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" content changed: updates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedProperties"},{"type":"text","text":", fires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.identify(userID:, properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with the new dictionary."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"u1\" → nil"},{"text":" (sign-out): clears both, fires ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stable userID and stable ","type":"text"},{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": no-op.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" is re-evaluated every non-analytics dispatch; dictionary equality decides whether to re-fire "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This keeps derived people-properties (subscription tier, paywall entitlements, feature flags) in sync with state without any explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".identify"},{"type":"text","text":" plumbing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When opted out, auto-identify is paused: neither ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedUserID"},{"type":"text","text":" nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastIdentifiedProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" is updated. Opting back in re-establishes identity correctly on the next dispatch."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Flushing","type":"heading","text":"Flushing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" awaits any pending fire-and-forget service calls spawned by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", then calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service.flush()"},{"type":"text","text":". Call this on app shutdown to avoid losing in-flight events:"}]},{"code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await store.analyticsPlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Implementing-an-AnalyticsService","type":"heading","text":"Implementing an `AnalyticsService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin is provider-agnostic. Your conformer is responsible for translating "},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" into whatever the backend SDK expects."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has five methods, all ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and non-throwing. Errors are the service’s responsibility: log them, queue for retry, drop them — whatever fits your backend’s reliability model. The plugin will not see them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typical Mixpanel conformer holds a reference to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.Instance"},{"type":"text","text":" and translates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsValue"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"MixpanelType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An Amplitude conformer holds an "},{"code":"Amplitude","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance and translates to "},{"code":"[String: Any]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note what the protocol does "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" require: no opt-out flag (the plugin handles that), no super-property machinery for "},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the plugin handles that), and no event batching policy (your call)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}]},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/swiduxmixpanelanalytics/":{"url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","type":"link","title":"DocC reference","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"DocC reference","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","title":"KeyValueStore","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","role":"article","title":"Add Analytics","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"title":"Macros","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"link","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide"}}}